:PNLGRP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME=SYNCTEST.Synchronize Test Library
:P.This command was created to sysnchronize a test data library with
the production data library. It acts a varification tool and a refresh
tool.
:P.To use as verification only, use option REFRESH(*NO), the default. Use
REFRESH(*YES) to refresh the files in the data library.
:P.The verification happens whether refreshing or not. If refreshing the
the verificaiton happens after the refersh to ensure the refresh worked
properly.
:P.The verification checkes to ensure that all data libraries exist in the
test library that are in the production library. It also ensures that no
file in the test library relates to the produciton library. Such as a
logical file or view pointing to the produciton library.
:p.The refresh operation deletes all logical files, views and indexes
in the testdata library. It then duplicates each table and physical file
from the production library into the test library. The it duplicates all
logical files, views and indexes from the production library to the test
library.
:p.All results are emailed to the address specified in the command.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SYNCTEST/PRDLIB'.PRDLIB - From (Production) Library
:XH3.PRDLIB - From (Production) Library
:P.This is the library to verify against and/or refersh from. Nothing
in this library is changed.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SYNCTEST/TSTLIB'.TESTLIB - To (Test) Library
:XH3.TESTLIB - To (Test) Library
:P.This is the library to compare to the production library and/or
refresh from.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SYNCTEST/REFRESH'.REFRESH - Refresh all data objects
:XH3.REFRESH - Refresh all data objects
:P.This options determines if the data objects in the test library are
rebuilt/refreshed. Se the extedned help for what this does.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SYNCTEST/EMAILTO'.EMAILTO - Email To
:XH3.EMAILTO - Email To
:P.Specifies the email address to send the results to.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SRJ/JOBNAME'.JOBNAME - Job Name
:XH3.JOBNAME - Job Name
:P.Specifies the name of the job used on the SBMJOB command. This
can be useful to see if the job is still running.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:EPNLGRP.
